// The kind the others start from (plan/design-two-systems.md, sections 9 to 11): every kind takes its handlers for
// the events it has none of its own for (`kind K from B` names another). It is not opened itself.
//
// - hole: a ticket resting at a hole (`...`) is put to the minder once something has happened on it since it was last
//   asked: a post not by coordd, an answer, a ticket under it closed (a kind's own hole is not asked on arrival; a
//   hole in a program the minder wrote is). The minder answers `shape` (shape.call): Rest, a Program to stand at the
//   hole (checked as an Edit there is), or Close(result). It never posts; each answer it gives is a logged line the
//   owner can undo. With nobody in the role, coordd answers the step itself, with one model call (shape.rs, the
//   minder where no agent holds the role); the NoWorker arm is reached only when the policy cannot be solved.
// - ask: an agent holding a step of the ticket asked, and waits in its turn (block_ask): a question to the lead, who
//   may pass it up to the owner; its answer is the asker's command's result. A lead filling it that waits on the
//   asker itself, through asks of its own (`coord ask`, a cycle: docket-machine `Machine::cycle`), is passed over, to
//   the owner.
// - owner_post: the owner's words landed on the ticket as a post (a thread's first words, a Place, a pick, a Move,
//   the owner's own post; not words that answer a step owed to the owner, design-two-systems §13). While this runs
//   the post is held: no agent is given it. `tell AGENTS p` wakes those agents and informs every other agent on the
//   ticket; `drop p` withdraws it (the owner sees it struck through). Ending with neither, the post goes as policy
//   says. Ours: the owner's answers to what a post asks go to whom they were typed to (paper-research m1437: no
//   call for them); words that name someone go to them, and so do words on a ticket nobody else is on, and words typed
//   to nobody on a ticket with one agent go to that agent (paper-research m1418: no call for them); otherwise the
//   watcher says whom they are for (route.call), and when it cannot tell, the owner does (clarify.call), by a press:
//   whom it is for, or drop it. When route says the words go on from a post of his just before them (its `joins`, the
//   thread's holder: his p586 and p587 on N-1104, 20 Nov), `tell … joining` keeps that post on them, and those told
//   read which post they go on from; one still theirs to answer is answered with them (hs-ls N-1446 p38). His typed
//   words are held first (`gather`, E1b; the owner, N-1445 p9: "hold them for 15s by default and ask a docket program
//   to split them"): for the policy's `lapse-after("gather", N)` from his first post (while he types in the thread's
//   box it waits on, up to the policy's `lapse-at-most("gather", N)` from his first post: the 60 s ceiling,
//   proto-engine's, with paper-research's yes at N-1446 p40), or until his "Send now" (on a slowed thread only that),
//   his next posts on the ticket join the first, and everything below reads his burst, their words joined, as one
//   message; route may then split it between agents by whole posts (its `Split`), each part told to its own (a split of
//   more than 20 parts is not split: every post of it goes to every agent on the ticket, each once). A post of the
//   burst that carries his own choice (its @NAMEs, the post it answers) goes to exactly whom he chose, and one that
//   says `@all` goes as a lone `@all` does, one agent taking it by claims (`p.claimed`, before anything else;
//   proto-lead N-1446 p475): when the burst's posts do not all carry one same choice, route reads them all and coordd
//   takes only an answer that sends each such post there (`p.chosen`; consult-3 N-1446 p281, proto-reader p307,
//   proto-lead p325); when route cannot tell whom the posts left are for, those he chose for go where he chose and he
//   is asked about the rest; when every post carries a choice, nothing is asked (`p.left`, proto-reader p445). With no
//   hold in the policy `gather` is his post at once, as before. Words he types on the thread while a question to him
//   waits are a post of their own, with their own names, and the post he did not answer is handed to every agent on the
//   thread (the machine, `hand_unanswered`; paper-research N-807.p78): nothing withdraws a post of his but his own
//   "drop it". Words that say `@all` reach every agent on the ticket and one of them takes it (consult-lead N-1158 post
//   1; the owner, N-1104 post 26: "reach all but only 1 needs to claim it eh so be smart about it"): the policy's
//   decision `claims` (claims.call) says which one is handed it, and `tell` informs the others, who see it at their
//   next delivery; the first answer to it, by any of them, is the claim, and another agent's answer after that is
//   refused. Another team writes its own; a kind replaces it with its own `when owner_post`.
/// the kind the others take their handlers from; it is not opened itself
kind base
  pattern
    ...
  when hole(h) do
    try {
      k <- step role minder shape(this);
      continue k
    } handle {
      NoWorker(w) => ...
    }
  when ask(q) do
    a <- open question(q.text, q.context);
    reply q a
  when owner_post(p) do
    // `p`, as before E1b: a recorded handler's program runs with this name bound, and every one recorded before reads
    // `p` (a replay of one gave his post to nobody under `first`: proto-engine N-1446)
    p <- gather p;
    // his `@all` in a burst whose posts carry different choices (`p.claimed`) goes as a lone `@all` does: the policy's
    // claims says which one agent is handed it, the others informed (proto-lead N-1446 p475); `p.text` is then the
    // burst's other posts, what the holder reads
    _ <- match p.claimed {
      none => return ()
      c =>
        taker <- decide claims(c.to, c.text);
        tell [taker] c.posts
    };
    r <- match p.all {
      none =>
        match p.answers {
          none =>
            match p.names {
              // a burst whose posts carry different choices of his (`p.chosen`): each post where he chose, the holder
              // deciding the posts left (`p.left`), and with none left nothing is asked (proto-reader N-1446 p445)
              [] => match (p.chosen, p.naming, p.others) {
                ([], _, []) => return To(p.naming)
                ([], [], [a]) => return To([a])
                _ =>
                  match p.left.posts {
                    [] => return Split(p.chosen)
                    _ => step watcher route(p.text, p.naming, p.others)
                  }
              }
              _ => return To(p.naming)
            }
          _ => return To(p.naming)
        }
      everyone =>
        match everyone {
          [] => return To(p.naming)
          _ =>
            taker <- decide claims(everyone, p.text);
            return To([taker])
        }
    };
    match r {
      To(as, j) => tell as p joining j
      Split(parts) =>
        try {
          _ <- for part in parts up to 20 {
            tell part.to part.posts
          };
          return ()
        } handle {
          Exhausted => tell p.agents p
        }
      Unclear(why) =>
        // his own choices go where he chose first; he is asked only about the posts left (proto-reader N-1446 p445)
        try {
          _ <- for c in p.chosen up to 20 {
            tell c.to c.posts
          };
          w <- step owner clarify(p.left.text, why, p.agents);
          match w {
            Send(as) => tell as p
            Drop => drop p
            Again(t) => tell p.agents p
          }
        } handle {
          Exhausted => tell p.agents p
        }
    }
